  "implementationDetails": {
    "audioStrategy": "Phase 3 completes the instrument on one AudioContext. The three recorded, bundled, offline piano sample sets (Grand, Upright, Electric) are unchanged from Phase 2. Every other sound is live synthesis, declared in generatedSources: the organ (four models built from sine partials, percussion, key click, vibrato and chorus), the synth (fourteen required waveforms, filters, envelopes, LFO, voice modes), and the Phase 2 piano synthesis and fallback. Generated buffers (the synth white-noise loop, the organ key-click burst, and the reverb impulses) are generated at run time and are never described as recordings. Every sound reaches the Phase 2 graph: organ and synth chains with their own six-unit effect chains, the shared Rotary, master gain, and limiter.",
